# Tekton Pipelines — pinned source reference (cluster-substrate phase 4).
#
# The release manifest itself is ~1.6 MB of generated YAML and is deliberately
# NOT vendored here: committing it would bury real configuration under a wall of
# upstream output, and it is reproducible byte-for-byte from the URL below.
# What IS tracked is the pin — the exact version, URL and checksum — which is
# the part that carries intent.
#
# Applied by copying the fetched file to
# /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/manifests/tekton-pipelines.yaml, where k3s
# auto-deploy reconciles it.
#
# Track: CURRENT (v1.15.x), not the operator's LTS line (v1.6.x). The
# infrastructure document names choosing accidentally as a risk; current is
# chosen deliberately, for the same version-currency reason that justified
# self-hosting k3s rather than taking a provider's trailing version.
#
# NOTE: this is not on the GCS path the Tekton docs usually cite —
# storage.googleapis.com/tekton-releases/pipeline/previous/v1.15.0/release.yaml
# returns 404, and only the unpinned .../pipeline/latest/release.yaml resolves
# there. The GitHub release asset is the pinned source.
version: v1.15.0
url: https://github.com/tektoncd/pipeline/releases/download/v1.15.0/release.yaml
sha256: 9b1bfe474da43d4e7e9993e5c2b67ef0966b0a513de51f25087bc1118a5f49d3
